workedExample.problem:
Two ways to check whether a list has any repeated value. Give the time and extra-space growth of each:
```python
def has_repeat_slow(values):
    for i in range(len(values)):
        for j in range(i + 1, len(values)):
            if values[i] == values[j]:
                return True
    return False

def has_repeat_fast(values):
    seen = set()
    for v in values:
        if v in seen:
            return True
        seen.add(v)
    return False
```

